> they say that music hath charms to soothe the stubborn drawbridge. okay, but
> i haven't found or come across a musical instrument other than a drum in the
> current game that i'm playing (i've seen instruments before so i know they
> exist). the drum apparently isn't musical enough for the drawbridge, are
> there other non-obvious ways to open it.

Zapping a wand of opening at the drawbridge somewhat obvious.  In
3.0f, a wand of striking will also break down doors and drawbridges,
but you'd still have to cross the moat.  (Not hard, the giants'll be
along presently with just the thing.)  There's also a back door, if
you can traverse the moat to the other side.

> i was tempted to let a vortex carry me across the moat somehow but i
> figured it might drop me in the water and i reasoned that that would
> be fatal given the mysterious forces on that level.

Good thinking.

> Nethack3.x version number confusion. i was under the impression that after
> the second patch level nethack3 was upgraded to version 3.0f. i've seen
> references to nethack3.1 and nethack3.2 and surely these are premature at
> this time. [the Troll biting stuff occurred in version 3.0e].

Some people have inaccurately referred to Version 3.0e Patchlevel 1 as
3.1, and Version 3.0f Patchlevel 2 as 3.2.  Some refer to them as
3.0.1 and 3.0.2, which is closer.  But officially, the progression is
3.0e, 3.0e PL1, 3.0f PL2.  The next patch will be 3.0f PL3, unless
dramatic changes are made or a major feature is added, in which case
it'd be 3.0g PL3.  Clear?

